kit: site-quality
version: 0.1.0
source: bamr87/bamr87 templates/site-quality/
seeded-by: tools/fanout.sh --kit site-quality (Jekyll repos only; needs a root _config.yml)
files: site-quality.yml, site-quality.template.yml, site-quality.schema.json, fixtures/
targets: site-quality.yml -> .github/workflows/site-quality.yml; site-quality.template.yml -> .github/site-quality.yml (only when absent); site-quality.schema.json and fixtures/ stay in the hub
spec: specs/QUALITY.md "Site quality" (UPS-QA-60..63, draft, rollout warn); checker contract specs/QUALITY.contract.yml; reusable workflow .github/workflows/site-quality.yml (runtime .github/site-quality/); cross-refs UPS-FE-50 (WCAG AA), UPS-FE-53 (Lighthouse budgets)
tests: templates/site-quality/test_site_quality_kit.py (stdlib + PyYAML; jsonschema used when installed); .github/site-quality/tests (node --test); .github/workflows/site-quality-selftest.yml (pass + fail fixture sites, url mode)
updated: 2026-10-04
changelog: |
  0.1.0 — initial kit, lifted from the two green implementations rather than
  invented: bamr87/lifehacker.dev#683 and bamr87/it-journey#790 (both add
  .github/workflows/site-quality.yml + .github/site-quality/ with lighthouserc,
  axe and pa11y contrast scripts and a local server). What the kit adds is the
  fleet contract: ONE reusable workflow with a build mode (build the Jekyll
  site against a fresh theme resolved to a commit SHA, serve _site) and a url
  mode (scan live URLs), exact-pinned tools with a committed lockfile, a
  caller config validated by a JSON Schema (schema: site-quality/v1, quoted dates, an
  allowlist where every known issue carries rule, selector and/or page,
  reason, issue link and until date), and lenient defaults: as seeded, no
  scan finding fails a caller (an invalid config or a failed build still
  does).
notes: |
  - Additive-only, like every kit: an existing .github/site-quality.yml is
    never overwritten; the caller workflow is refreshed by --upgrade only when
    it matches the kit or an archive/ snapshot.
  - Repos that built their own site-quality workflow (lifehacker.dev,
    it-journey) migrate by hand: move their thresholds into
    .github/site-quality.yml, then replace the workflow with the caller.
  - Callers pin @v1 (never a custom tag). The runner always comes from the
    same hub commit as the workflow (job.workflow_sha, else hub-ref, else v1).
  - Snapshot to archive/ before editing site-quality.yml or the template.
